I seem to be on a roll as I've managed to ascend three of my last five
characters played. This was the second of the three where I avoided
genociding any monsters, and as a bonus, avoided polypiling. The latter
may not sound like as much of a challenge, but to a polypile-addict
like myself, it was really hard not to give into temptation. I also did
not change form or wish for any artifacts, but I almost never do these
things (unless unintentionally if I step on a polytrap before getting
magic resistance).

To be fair, I started the game with a spellbook of identify, which made
me much less worried about genociding flayers; besides, my Int was low
so I wanted to kill and eat some. And I found so much of my ascension
kit in the dungeon (including a bit from one bones pile), I hardly
needed to wish for anything, much less polypile. In fact, the only
wishes I made were for silver dragon scale (I had made my own gray
scale earlier, but decided to ditch the shield of reflection for better
spellcasting) and magic marker. I found at least three other magic
markers, six amulets of life saving (none were used), a magic lamp
(kept for light only), and a wand of wishing in Gehennom of all places
(also not used, but this is part of why I go down every pathway on
every level of Gehennom).

I've played plenty of Priestesses before but never an Elven one; not
much of a difference, though higher max strength would have been nice;
being Chaotic was helpful in Gehennom, especially coming back out. I
used +6 Frost Brand with +6 Stormbringer as a backup only for vampires
etc., and plenty of magic missile spells (which worked well -
especially for the sea monsters and flayers I normally genocide -
despite being restricted in that class). Rodney didn't bother me too
much; though my wands of death missed him more often than I would have
liked, I'd found several and could have recharged if needed. Elemental
planes were pretty easy, and Astral was easiest in memory as none of
the Riders got close enough to touch me; the first altar I arrived at
was the right one, and I was done.

